# Release signing credentials for the app module.
#
# Copy this file to keystore.properties in the repository root and fill in the
# real values. keystore.properties is gitignored: never commit it, and never
# commit the .jks file either.
#
# Gradle reads keystore.properties first, then falls back to TRIPLOGGER_*
# environment variables (TRIPLOGGER_STORE_FILE, TRIPLOGGER_STORE_PASSWORD,
# TRIPLOGGER_KEY_ALIAS, TRIPLOGGER_KEY_PASSWORD) for CI or to keep no secret
# file on disk. Every value must come from one of the two places.
#
# storeFile: absolute path, or a path relative to the repository root.
# storeFile, storePassword and keyAlias are required.
# keyPassword is optional: it defaults to storePassword, which is always the
# right answer for PKCS12 stores (.jks files exported by Android Studio are
# PKCS12). Set it only for a JKS store with a distinct key password.
#
# Values are read by java.util.Properties: do NOT wrap them in quotes (the
# quotes would become part of the password) and escape a literal backslash as \\.
storeFile=/absolute/path/to/upload-key.jks
storePassword=change-me
keyAlias=change-me
